tional buildings. The gasometers are four former gas tanks, built as part of the Vienna…"],["Remise - Verkehrsmuseum der Wiener Linien","sight",48.19678,16.40671,"Ludwig-Koessler-Platz","Wed 09:00-18:00; Sat Sun 10:00-18:00","","","","r","This museum in a former depot houses a comprehensive collection of vintage vehicles explaining the history of Viennese public transport. The exhibits include horse-drawn streetcars from 1868, a steam tram set from 1885, many electric…"],["Sankt Marxer Friedhof","sight",48.18253,16.40131,"Leberstrasse 6-8","Apr-Sep: 06:30-20:00, Oct-Mar: 06:30-18:00","","","","r","This historic cemetery was in use from 1784 until 1874. Mozart was buried here in an unmarked pauper's grave in 1791; the tombstone dates from a later period, after his grave was tentatively identified. The Bezirksmuseum Landstraße…"],["Arena","activity",48.1879,16.41296,"Baumgasse 80","","","","","r","The arena is one of the biggest concert and alternative culture places. The slaughterhouse got squatted in 1976 and operates since as culture center. FM4 hosts here its annual birthday party. The programme lists the performing artists.…"],["Amon","restaurant",48.19552,16.40864,"Schlachthausgasse 13","Mon–Sat 10:30–24:00, Sun 11:00–16:00","","","","r","The restaurant serves seasonal Viennese food typically of course plates with large quantities. The cellar is a vinothek with a good selection of Austrian wines."],["O'Connor's Old Oak","restaurant",48.18892,16.40006,"Rennweg 95/2/1","Mon–Fri 10:00–01:00, Sat Sun 13:00–24:00","","","","r","Gareth \"Gaz\" Smith is cooking here daily, hence this Irish pub may serve the best Irish food in Vienna (not only legendary fish and chips)."]]}